I know English is illogical in lots of places, but this is one of the
mistakes made most often. Contrary to one's gut feelings, "belonging to
it" does not become "it's", but "its" instead. As opposed to "John's" for
"belonging to John", "the baker's" for "belonging to the baker", etc.

"It's" actually means "it is" or "it has".

